1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roars]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[narrator]
Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
[squeaking]

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

6
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Evil haunts.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The mysterious unknown.

10
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words...

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,000
are called...

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hunters.

13
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,000
[theme music playing]

14
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Guess I’ll let go, then.

15
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Hold on, don’t let go!
I’m awake!

16
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,000
I’m awake!

17
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
[Majitani groans]

18
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,000
[clock beeps]

19
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Even so,
you have only twenty hours remaining.

20
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,000
I know. But at least now we’re in
a better position with a two-one lead.

21
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Now,

22
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
let's keep this ball rolling.

23
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,000
The choice is yours.
So, what’s it gonna be?

24
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:31,000
TROUBLE x WITH x THE GAMBLE

25
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
[narrator] In the five-on-five battle
with the prisoners,

26
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Gon and friends lead two-to-one.

27
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
They’re one win away from victory.

28
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Round four is a series of bets
with time as the currency.

29
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
What will they bet on next?

30
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Well? Let’s hear it.
What’s the next wager gonna be, huh?

31
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Or did you lose your nerve
when I saw through your little scam?

32
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
[Leroute chuckles]
Very well.

33
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
LEROUTE 112-YEAR SENTENCE ILLEGAL GAMBLING
AND ENDANGERED SPECIES TRAFFICKING

34
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,000
[Leorio]
Damn, she's really cute.

35
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
[laughs bashfully]

36
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,000
What a pervert.
I hear his heartbeat from here.

37
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
I don’t like where this is heading.

38
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,000
All right.

39
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
What do you say we place bets on
whether I’m a man or a woman?

40
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Huh?

41
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
What’s the matter?
That isn’t a problem, is it?

42
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,000
[Leorio]
Uh, no.

43
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
She is definitely a woman.

44
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Or maybe she’s a cross-dresser?

45
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,000
No way. She’s gotta be a woman.

46
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Fine, I accept.

47
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,000
But what if I bet you’re a man?

48
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
How exactly are you gonna prove
you’re not?

49
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Oh, right.

50
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:53,000
I promise to let you examine
every square inch of my body.

51
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Now, will that satisfy you?

52
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,000
[Leorio]
Yeah....

53
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Her body?

54
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,000
[laughs excitedly in his head]

55
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,000
He’s already chosen.
He’ll bet she’s a man.

56
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,000
-Yeah.
-[Gon] Huh? Why?

57
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
[Leorio]
I've made up my mind.

58
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
And I’ll wager ten hours
that you’re actually a man!

59
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
[Leroute scoffs]

60
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,000
I knew it.

61
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Dirty, stinkin’ old man…

62
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
But... how did you know?

63
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,000
[Leorio]
This way,

64
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
even if I’m wrong and she is a woman

65
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,000
still get to check out her body!

66
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Either way,
talk about a win-win situation!

67
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Actually, I hope I’m wrong!

68
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
Do you get it now?

69
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Yeah, I do.

70
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Okay, reveal the answer!

71
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,000
That’s too bad. I’m really a woman.

72
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:52,000
[gulps]
Oh, you are, huh?

73
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,000
Well, want to check for yourself?

74
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Well, don’t mind if I do.
I mean, just to be fair, of course.

75
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:05,000
[Leorio laughing]

76
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:08,000
[beeping]

77
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
[Leorio]
I regret nothing.

78
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
[Gon sighs]

79
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
It is physically painful to watch this.

80
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
[Tonpa]
He's going to lose.

81
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
No question. She can already see
right through his strategy.

82
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,000
He’s betting safe.

83
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
It’s obvious.
Hedging his bets to minimize the damage.

84
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,000
He’s the kind of gambler

85
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:33,000
who tries to avoid losing
instead of trying to win.

86
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
That kind of betting
never takes home the prize.

87
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,000
[Leorio chuckling]

88
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Sorry to say it, boys, but Leorio
just doesn’t have what it takes.

89
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,000
[Leroute] I thought so.

90
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,000
His gambling style is
nothing to worry about.

91
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:52,000
If he keeps playing that way,
he doesn’t have a prayer.

92
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,000
[chuckles]

93
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Well?
Your turn to pick what we bet on next.

94
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
So what do you wanna wager?

95
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
[Leorio]
This is no time to celebrate.

96
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:08,000
I've only got ten hours left to bet with.

97
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Leorio has no room for error.

98
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Losing the next bet would tie the score
up at two-to-two.

99
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
And then we lose 50 hours,

100
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:20,000
leaving very little time
to clear the tower.

101
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,000
[Gon] Leorio.

102
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Okay, what to bet on…

103
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:29,000
I can’t afford to lose
but I can’t think of a sure-fire win.

104
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Hey, I got it!

105
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:34,000
We’ll bet on whether I’m a really man
or just a woman in disguise

106
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
No, that’s never gonna work.
Gotta think of something else.

107
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Keep it to yourself, old man.

108
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,000
Thinking out loud
isn’t how you plan a strategy!

109
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,000
I know.

110
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
-[Gon] Leorio!
-Huh?

111
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,000
How ‘bout you bet on whether or not
you’re a teenager?

112
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Give me a break, Gon.

113
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:54,000
There’s no way I look that old
and you all know it!

114
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
I’m clearly a teenager!

115
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
He's... a teenager?

116
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,000
Wow, he looks like an old man.

117
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,000
All right! I know what we’re betting on.

118
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Let’s bet on who’ll win
rock paper scissors!

119
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,000
[giggles]
Why not.

120
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Is he serious?

121
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Why did he have to pick
such a difficult wager?

122
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
Wait.
What’s so hard about rock paper scissors?

123
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,000
[Leorio scoffs]
Just so happens,

124
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
rock paper scissors is my specialty.

125
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
In fact, I just played a tournament
in the shopping district

126
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
and I won a gourmet vacation.

127
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,000
Let's see.

128
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:37,000
So for my wager, I’ve got eighty hours
that say I’ll win, okay?

129
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Eh... Did you just say 80?

130
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
That’s not a problem, is it?

131
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
I'm free to bet however much I want.

132
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,000
Uh...

133
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,000
I guess there's no rule against it.

134
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Perfect. And if you lose,

135
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
I can only take ten from you
since that’s all you have left.

136
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,000
So don't worry.

137
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:57,000
[Leorio]
She doesn't need to bet 80 hours.

138
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Ten's plenty.

139
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
I mean, what if she loses?

140
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Is she that confident
in her rock paper scissors skills?

141
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:10,000
[Leroute] As expected,
he's starting to stress out. [giggles]

142
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
I can read him like an open book.

143
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,000
While the rules
of rock paper scissors are simple,

144
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,000
the game itself can be incredibly complex.

145
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
From the perspective of probability,

146
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,000
you only stand a one-in-three chance
of losing any given round.

147
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:30,000
But if your opponent can predict
your reasoning

148
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,000
and control your reactions,

149
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:34,000
your chance of losing
increases dramatically.

150
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,000
In short, this is a game of wits

151
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
and Leorio is pretty lacking
in that department.

152
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,000
I see.

153
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,000
[Leorio]
Okay, I'm ready.

154
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
[chuckles]

155
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Hey, what's so funny?

156
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,000
It’s just I can already tell
what you’re going to use.

157
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
I’m something of a mind reader, you see.

158
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:58,000
That is a lie.

159
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:02,000
You can bluff all you want, but it’ll take
a lot more than that to scare me!

160
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,000
You’ll believe it soon…

161
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:11,000
[Leroute giggles] Just like I planned.
One blatant lie and he's losing it.

162
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
[Leorio]
Can she really read minds?

163
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:17,000
No, she’s lying. She’s gotta be.

164
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,000
But what if she isn't?

165
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,000
Leorio will use rock.

166
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,000
You ready?

167
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
-And... rock, paper, scissors.
-Scissors.

168
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,000
You were right.

169
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Good guess, Kurapika.

170
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Leorio was nervous,

171
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:39,000
leading him to avoid any actions
that involved opening up.

172
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,000
She's good.

173
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
She’s doing everything she can
to make him uncomfortable

174
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
and less likely to use paper.

175
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:51,000
So, she sticks to rock,
ensuring either a win or a draw.

176
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,000
Like I said,

177
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Rock-paper-scissors is
actually a mind game.

178
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,000
Now I see.

179
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Hang on.

180
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,000
We both used rocks,
so that was a draw, wasn't it?

181
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,000
So what if it was?

182
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Ha! I knew it!

183
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:10,000
You were lying about being able
to read my mind!

184
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:14,000
If you really were a psychic,
then you would have beaten me! Right?!

185
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,000
[giggles]

186
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,000
[Leorio]
What are you laughing at?

187
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:21,000
I gave you that tie on purpose.
You’re welcome.

188
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Quit lying!

189
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
Have you forgotten already?

190
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:27,000
We’re trying to stall you here
for as long as possible.

191
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,000
If I really wanted to,

192
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,000
I could force a series of draws
that would last indefinitely.

193
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,000
But why?

194
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:39,000
I’m sure that wouldn’t be half as fun
as toying with you.

195
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:42,000
But I’ll end it after this.

196
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Well, what will you use next?

197
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:49,000
Come on, think hard. [laughs]

198
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Damn it!

199
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,000
[Leroute]
Yes, that's it. .

200
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,000
Worry. Fret.

201
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,000
[Kurapika]
Worrying, fretting.

202
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,000
Whenever someone’s confidence
is shattered,

203
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
they begin to crave reassurance.

204
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,000
See? That’s obviously
what’s happening to Leorio.

205
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,000
He'll use the same play,

206
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:12,000
play or something stronger
to regain his confidence.

207
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
I see what she's doing.

208
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:18,000
She's trying to get Leorio to choose
either rock or paper.

209
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,000
Correct.

210
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Using paper means
she’s certain not to lose.

211
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:26,000
Then Leorio’s gotta stay one step ahead!

212
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Indeed.

213
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
And if he were calmer,
he might actually be able to.

214
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:34,000
-[Gon] Leorio!
-Now what?

215
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Listen! If you want to win,
you’ve gotta play scissors!

216
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:39,000
Scissors, what?

217
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:43,000
[giggles]
Go ahead, try.

218
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,000
[Leorio] But if I do,
she's just going to use rock.

219
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:52,000
No. She’ll go a step further
and choose paper.

220
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:55,000
Unless she goes even further
and picks scissors.

221
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Or she might jump ahead
and go straight to rock…

222
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
[screams]
What is happening!

223
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,000
Here we go.

224
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Here comes the draw!

225
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,000
[beeping]

226
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,000
[cries out]
I win, yay!

227
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
[laughing]

228
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Amazing.
This game’s really hard.

229
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
And now the score’s two-two.

230
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Even worse, we have far less time

231
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,000
now that we’ve lost the 50 hours
he gambled with.

232
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:39,000
[Leorio] Sorry, I thought I was
a rock paper scissors pro.

233
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
[Tonpa scoffs]
Pretty pathetic showing.

234
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,000
What did you say?

235
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,000
Yeah,
I guess I can't argue with you there.

236
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:57,000
Okay. So how much time do they have left?
How did I do?

237
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:02,000
[chuckles]
Fifty-nine hours, forty-five minutes.

238
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Not bad.
By my calculations, that means

239
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:09,000
they’ve now got fewer than ten hours
to reach the bottom.

240
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
It doesn't matter how much time they have.

241
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,000
[gasping]

242
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:19,000
[man] It doesn't matter
because my opponent is about to die.

243
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:35,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

244
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:39,000
ROCK-PAPER-SCISSORS

245
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
So the final round is upon us.

246
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,000
I guess that means I’m up.

247
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
Huh? Wait, Killua?

248
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
What does that mean?

249
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,000
Damn, this sucks!

250
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:54,000
I really needed to win my round.
It’s all my fault!

251
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,000
Gon, your buddy, here, is pissing me off.

252
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Take it easy.

253
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Don’t throw in the towel.

254
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:02,000
We don’t even know
what the next contest is yet.

255
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
But if it’s something
like doing math in your head,

256
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,000
I’m totally surrendering.

257
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,000
Hey, you’re right

258
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:10,000
If the next opponent’s a weakling,
we might still have a chance!

259
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,000
[Bendot]
That kid's their last member.

260
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,000
I didn’t think he’d draw the short straw.

261
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:19,000
That poor thing. He’s still so young.

262
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:23,000
[Lippo] I did everything I could
to avoid using him.

263
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:27,000
However, the Hunter Exam isn’t the time
or the place

264
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,000
for showing mercy.

265
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:31,000
If he dies, well, that’s fate.

266
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Removing his handcuffs.

267
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,000
[handcuffs click]

268
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:52,000
I don’t get it.
What are you guys scared of?

269
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,000
Stop, you idiot.

270
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,000
He doesn’t look all that terrifying to me.

271
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
That's all ancient histor--

272
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
[gasping]

273
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,000
It's that guy...

274
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:33,000
You know him?

275
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,000
We should just take the loss.

276
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
Killua, you can't fight this guy.

277
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,000
Why not?

278
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:42,000
[Leorio] Johness, the Dissector...

279
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,000
SERIAL KILLER SERVING A 968-YEAR SENTENCE

280
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:46,000
The worst mass murderer
in Zaban’s history.

281
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,000
He chose his victims at random.

282
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:55,000
It was all over the news.
146 people.

283
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Men, women, young, old, all slaughtered.

284
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:02,000
Each of the victims had
one thing in common.

285
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:06,000
He murdered every single one of them
with his bare hands.

286
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:11,000
His grip was infamous.
The raw power in his fingers alone…

287
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,000
It was unreal.

288
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:18,000
It’s been ages
since I last touched human flesh.

289
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,000
He’s a complete psychopath.
You don’t have to fight him!

290
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,000
There's always next year, right?.

291
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,000
Hey, Killua!

292
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,000
Killua!

293
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:37,000
What the hell?!
Wasn’t he listening to a word I just said?

294
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Let him go, Leorio.

295
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,000
He might have a plan
we don't know about.

296
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,000
[music playing]

297
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,000
How do you want to do this?

298
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,000
[Johness]
Do this?

299
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,000
You have the wrong idea.

300
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:02,000
See, you’re about to be
on the wrong side of a one-sided massacre.

301
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:06,000
I don't care about the Exam
or reducing my sentence.

302
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,000
All I want is to hear you scream.

303
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Really? Fine.

304
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,000
We'll just keep fighting
until one of us dies.

305
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,000
That's right.
A battle to the death.

306
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,000
-Soon... I'll tear your body apart
-[wind rustles]

307
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,000
with just my bare hands, you got it?

308
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:30,000
[heart beats]

309
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
[gasping]

310
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,000
[struggles to breathe]

311
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,000
What happened?

312
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:49,000
Why am I so cold?

313
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:55,000
[heart beats]

314
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,000
That's mine...
[grunts]

315
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
It belongs to me.

316
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,000
[beating grows weaker]

317
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
Give it back. Give it to me.

318
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:10,000
[beating slows]

319
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,000
[gasping weakly]

320
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,000
[beeping]

321
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:34,000
So, that's three wins for us.

322
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:35,000
We move on, right?

323
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:38,000
That's right. Yeah, you guys win.

324
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,000
By the way,

325
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,000
you must be itching for some action.

326
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,000
You didn't get to fight.

327
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,000
How about it?
Want to take me on?

328
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Thanks but no thanks.

329
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Suit yourself.

330
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:59,000
Whoa, who is this kid, anyway?

331
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:01,000
That's right, you guys don't know?

332
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:02,000
Wait. Know what?

333
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Killua's family. He says
they're a bunch of elite assassins.

334
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:10,000
[surprised gasp]
Did you say elite assassins?

335
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,000
[Killua] I'm back.

336
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,000
What?

337
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:17,000
Just... good work out there!

338
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:29,000
[Lippo]
Please cross the bridge.

339
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:32,000
[over PA] On the other side,
you'll find a small room.

340
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:35,000
That's where you'll be spending
the 50 hours you gambled away.

341
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Well, come on.

342
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
-[Gon] Mm-hmm.
-All right, sure.

343
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:04,000
[voice over PA] Gittarackur,
applicant 301, is the second to pass.

344
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Time elapsed, 12 hours and two minutes.

345
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:11,000
Something told me
you'd already passed the finish line.

346
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,000
[Hanzo]
All right!!

347
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:18,000
-[over PA] Applicant 294, is the third...
-I'm the first one to finish!

348
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,000
What the...?

349
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
-...twelve hours and three minutes.
-Oh!

350
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,000
I don't believe it.

351
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:24,000
I came in third place.

352
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:27,000
[rumbling]

353
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:29,000
[beeping]

354
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Oh, come on, give me a break.

355
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:35,000
Can't believe we've got to sit around here
for 50 hours.

356
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,000
-Killua.
-Huh?

357
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,000
Can you tell me how
that technique works?

358
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,000
What do you mean "technique".

359
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,000
The one you used
to instantly remove his heart.

360
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:48,000
Oh, that one.
Well, it wasn't a technique, really.

361
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,000
I just ripped it out.

362
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,000
[Kurapika] That's all?

363
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:57,000
To be honest... I did manipulate
my body some. Made it a lot easier.

364
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:59,000
Whoa! Your nails!

365
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Oh, wow.

366
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:05,000
Mass murderers talk big,
but they're still just amateurs.

367
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,000
I used to be a professional.

368
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:11,000
But my old man would have done
a lot better.

369
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:14,000
When he takes a heart,
there's not even a drop of blood.

370
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:17,000
[laughs nervousy]
That's good to know. Thanks, kid.

371
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,000
[Kurapika]
At least he's on our side.

372
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:26,000
All right then,
we've got more than two days.

373
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,000
So what do you want to do?

374
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:29,000
We've got to do something.

375
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:32,000
First, let's search the room to see
if there's anything to play with.

376
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,000
Okay.

377
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,000
Kids! Not a care in the world, huh?

378
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:40,000
Time to take a load off.

379
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:47,000
[narrator] Gon's team of five passed
the trial

380
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:48,000
with three wins and two losses.

381
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,000
But now must spend their
50-hour penalty here.

382
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:56,000
Unfortunately,
they're running out of time.

383
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:57,000
[beeping]

384
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,000
[theme music plays]

385
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,000
[Gon] Next time.
"Final Test of Resolve."

386
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,000
You have to think like a fish!

387
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,000
-[Killua] Seriously?
-[Gon] Yep!
